From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "sh.chao" <sh.chao@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 13:05:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Veloce r25-3-0115: intern exact path-only clip runs

Treat pointer identity as the fast path for retained clips, then compare
pointer-distinct path-only clips by exact fill rule, point type, close flag,
and floating-point bits. Consecutive equivalent scopes retain one immutable
representative without changing source order or the canonical PDFium object
model.

This removes redundant clip installation and its forced draw-batch flush for
producers that emit the same clip before every path. Text clips and every
structurally different or malformed clip remain distinct and therefore keep
the existing fail-closed replay behavior. The comparison allocates no memory,
uses no tolerance or page classifier, and the retained-program budget remains
unchanged.

Add unit coverage for pointer-distinct equivalent clips and for A/B/A clip
transitions, bump the immutable program format, and expose exact comparison
counters. On Error.pdf pages 2/3, the expected proof is 28,071 native fills
with `clipRuns=1`, about 110 bounded dispatches instead of 28,071, and
unchanged pixels.
---
